WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.234
"Pros and Cons of Raw Food Diets"

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:10.280
Is it better to eat
our vegetables raw or cooked?

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:12.160
If you're thinking raw,
you're right!

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:14.480
But if you guessed cooked,
you're also right.

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:16.640
A number of nutrients,
like vitamin C,

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:18.960
are partially destroyed
by cooking.

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:20.720
On the other hand,
some nutrients,

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:22.480
like lycopene in tomatoes,

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:25.200
become more absorbable
upon cooking.

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:26.280
So, I advocate eating

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:29.080
a combination
of cooked and raw foods.

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:31.320
Check out this study
on long-term raw foodists.

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:32.480
This study was done in Europe,

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:35.920
so the "average Western diet"
here wasn't terrible,

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:38.800
about four servings
of fruits and vegetables a day;

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:42.040
versus a better so-called
"wholesome nutrition" diet

00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:44.560
of seven daily servings
of fruits and veggies,

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:48.320
both raw and cooked;
versus a raw food diet,

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:49.680
in which they ate, on average,

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:53.160
a whopping 17 servings
of fruits and veggies a day,

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:54.120
leading them to have

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:56.560
about three times
the beta-carotene intake

00:00:56.560 --> 00:00:59.000
compared
to the "average" eaters.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:00.040
But that's intake.

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:03.280
How much of it actually
got into their bloodstreams?

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:05.280
Blood beta-carotene
is considered to be

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:08.280
a surrogate marker for
fruit and vegetable consumption.

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:10.160
Some researchers even suggest

00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:12.720
if you tell them what your
blood beta-carotene level is,

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:15.480
they can tell you
what your health risk is.

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:18.680
So, who had the most
beta-carotene in their bodies?

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:22.920
Those eating 4 servings a day,
7, or 17?

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:26.160
It was the middle group--
the 7 daily servings group--

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:29.280
because cooking can boost
the absorption of phytonutrients

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:29.920
like beta-carotene.

00:01:31.160 --> 00:01:32.040
For example,

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:34.120
you get more beta-carotene
in your bloodstream

00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:35.280
eating cooked carrots

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:38.280
than you do eating
the same amount of raw carrots.

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:41.320
The raw foodists were eating
17 servings a day

00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:43.840
and basically had the same
amount of this phytonutrient

00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:46.560
reaching their internal organs
as those on the standard diet

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:49.880
getting 4 measly daily servings.

00:01:49.880 --> 00:01:52.920
Raw diets can be better than
junky vegan diets because

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:54.800
they're free of processed foods,

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:57.520
like potato chips
and sugary drinks.

00:01:57.520 --> 00:01:59.320
I couldn't find
any good evidence

00:01:59.320 --> 00:02:03.480
raw diets are superior to whole
food, plant-based diets, though.

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:05.800
A dietary survey of 141

00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:07.920
so-called
Hallelujah vegetarians,

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:10.880
following a mostly raw,
pure vegetarian diet,

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:15.640
found their raw food diets were
deficient in energy, protein,

00:02:15.640 --> 00:02:20.520
and vitamins B12 and D, calcium,
selenium, and zinc.

00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:23.520
A more recent survey
of strict raw food eaters

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:26.000
disturbingly found only
about half were supplementing

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:27.720
with vitamin B12

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:29.200
and were suffering
the consequences,

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:33.720
elevated levels of the toxic
metabolite homocysteine.

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:35.800
Most eating
the average Western diet

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:37.520
are getting
way too many calories,

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:40.200
but strict raw-foodists
may not get enough.

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:42.840
Being underweight, along
with nutritional deficiencies,

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:44.960
can cause women
to lose their period

00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:48.040
and could contribute
to osteoporosis.

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:51.840
Those eating 100 percent raw
can become too skinny.

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:54.640
And as many as half
may stop their period.

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:57.400
Does this actually have
an effect on bone mass?

00:02:57.400 --> 00:03:00.640
Raw foodists had significantly
lower bone mineral density

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:02.200
throughout
their entire skeleton,

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:06.000
and specifically
in their spine and hips.

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:07.800
There are a number
of seriously flawed myths

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:10.560
that circulate
within the raw foods community,

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:12.800
like we need to consume
live plant enzymes

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:15.160
which are deactivated
by cooking.

00:03:15.160 --> 00:03:18.240
Well, they're deactivated
by our stomach acid, too.

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:19.920
And since we're not plants,

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:22.240
we have no need
for plant enzymes.

00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:24.600
Our body makes all
the enzymes we need to function

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:26.960
from the protein we eat.

00:03:26.960 --> 00:03:30.680
If, for whatever reason,
you want to eat 100 percent raw,

00:03:30.680 --> 00:03:33.400
first, you must take
a B12 supplement

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:36.040
so you don't get
other nutrient deficiencies.

00:03:36.040 --> 00:03:38.120
Study Davis and Melina's
comprehensive guide

00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:39.880
on the subject.

00:03:39.880 --> 00:03:42.840
Also, a diet based
on modern cultivated fruits

00:03:42.840 --> 00:03:44.760
is not nutritionally adequate.

00:03:44.760 --> 00:03:46.800
They're a pale shadow
of the wild fruits

00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:49.600
eaten by our ape ancestors.

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:52.120
Make sure you rinse
the natural acids off your teeth

00:03:52.120 --> 00:03:53.880
after eating sour
fruits and beverages

00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:56.760
so you don't erode
your dental enamel.

00:03:56.760 --> 00:03:59.440
And also, make sure you
sufficiently chew your food

00:03:59.440 --> 00:04:02.320
so you don't block
your digestive tract.

00:04:02.320 --> 00:04:05.200
In fact, we explicitly recommend
against raw food diets

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:06.560
for young children,

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:08.440
as they just don't have
the stomach capacity

00:04:08.440 --> 00:04:11.040
to get adequate nutrition.

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:13.960
Although an all-raw food diet
can be healthy

00:04:13.960 --> 00:04:15.920
(this raw triple-ironman
showed no signs

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:18.840
of dietary deficiencies
or impaired health),

00:04:18.840 --> 00:04:20.280
there is no reliable evidence

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:22.440
to suggest that
it's more healthful

00:04:22.440 --> 00:04:27.507
than a diet of whole plant
foods--cooked or not.

